      "writtenOn": "2021-03-24T17:19:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "All of this is implemented by the OEM so it\u0027s from /vendor (via the KeyMaster or KeyMint HALs) and OEMs don\u0027t have to upgrade that partition (but some do) when they upgrade /system to Android 12. We will start requiring these features to be set starting with Android 12 and we\u0027ll check that that in CTS (CL:1626759).\n\nSo unfortunately this is more complicated than I like but there\u0027s nothing to do about this I\u0027m afraid. What I\u0027ve added in the latest PS is the following:\n\n This feature version is guaranteed to be set for all devices launching with\n Android 12 and may be set on devices launching with an earlier version. If\n the feature version is set, it will at least have the value 40. If it\u0027s not\n set the device may have a version of hardware-backed keystore but it may\n not support all features listed above.",
      "parentUuid": "047b42c2_4bb30aaa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3205,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 3206,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "e55be4061ded9849a2a931d88ed07d9868d8aded",
